    "description": "Wrongfully imprisoned on the eve of his wedding, a young sailor loses everything—his freedom, his future, and the woman he loves. From that moment begins one of the most extraordinary stories of betrayal, vengeance, transformation, and redemption ever written.\n\nEdmond Dantès is a promising young sailor whose life appears destined for happiness. He is about to marry the beautiful Mercédès and has earned the respect of his captain. But jealousy and political intrigue turn his good fortune into catastrophe. Betrayed by men he once trusted, Edmond is falsely accused of treason and secretly imprisoned in the formidable Château d’If.\n\nYears of isolation nearly destroy him. Then he meets Abbé Faria, a brilliant fellow prisoner who becomes his mentor and reveals the location of a hidden treasure. Armed with knowledge, patience, and a carefully constructed new identity, Edmond escapes and reenters society as the mysterious and immensely wealthy Count of Monte Cristo.\n\nFrom the salons of Paris to the shores of the Mediterranean, the Count methodically confronts those responsible for his downfall. Yet as his plans unfold, revenge proves more complicated than he imagined. Innocent lives are caught in the consequences, old loyalties are tested, and the line between justice and cruelty begins to disappear.\n\nAlexandre Dumas combines suspense, romance, political conspiracy, hidden identities, fortune, and moral conflict in a sweeping narrative that has captivated generations of readers. At once an adventure novel, a psychological drama, and a meditation on power and forgiveness, The Count of Monte Cristo remains one of the greatest works of popular literature ever written.\n\nRich in unforgettable characters and dramatic reversals, this timeless masterpiece asks whether any person has the right to judge and punish others—and whether true freedom can ever be achieved through revenge alone.",
